+29. **(rate card) The diff is computed in memory.** 5,500 rows against 5,500 rows keyed on the three row-identity columns `(mno_public_key, commercial_unit_public_key, polygon_id)` is a map comparison, not a set-based SQL diff and not a temp table (RC15). `polygon_start_date` is **out of the diff key** — it is descriptive (D-A9), and a polygon appears at most once per version, so a change to it is a **changed** row, not a remove + add. `polygon_end_date`, `state`, `district`, `service_code` and `rate_per_unit` are likewise compared as the row's payload, never part of the key. (The DB row-uniqueness index adds `ratecard_version_id`, §6.28 — that fourth column identifies a row across versions; the *within-version* diff key is these three.) Activation writes no rows (D-A7), so there is no set-based carry-forward statement. The in-memory diff keys rows on those three columns joined by a delimiter that cannot occur in them — **the same NUL-byte delimiter pm58's duplicate-key check uses** (`ROW_KEY_DELIMITER`, exported from `validation/product/ratecard.schema.ts`), reused via its `rateCardRowKey` helper rather than re-declared: two different delimiters in two files would be the beginning of two different answers. **Landed under pm62** (`services/product/ratecard/diff-versions.ts`, backed by two new reads added to `db/repositories/ratecard.ts` — `getAllRowsForVersion`/`getCurrentActiveRows` — so the diff's query budget (§3.23) holds at exactly two; pm62-diff.md's own header cites this rule as §6.33, this file's actual numbering has it at §6.29, a citation drift recorded here rather than silently reconciled in the spec file). **Which non-key columns count as "changed" was a doc-vs-doc conflict at authoring time** — pm62-diff.md's own D2 text named only `lkp_subscriber_ref_id` and `service_code`, narrower than this rule's list above; resolved with the user 2026-09-28 in favor of THIS rule (every non-key column compared, as written here) — pm62-diff.md D2 should be corrected